<txp:hide>
  u_debug — debugging aides for logged-in users (js/u_debug.js, styles in the kit's _debug.scss)

  <txp::u_debug title='form: thumb' />
    Put inside the form's outer element. Outputs an HTML comment marker, so it adds no
    element to the page. The script labels the marker's parent element with the title.
    A marker placed directly in <body> names the page and shows in the toolbar.

  The first call on a page also loads the script. The old attributes `breakpoints`,
  `toggle` and `class` are accepted and ignored: the toolbar now covers them.
</txp:hide>
<txp:if_logged_in>
<!--u_debug <txp:yield name="title" />-->
<txp:if_variable name="u_debug_js" value="1"><txp:else />
<txp:variable name="u_debug_js" value="1" />
<script src="<txp:page_url type="theme_path" />/js/u_debug.js?v=<txp:variable name="cache-buster" />" defer></script>
</txp:if_variable>
</txp:if_logged_in>
